<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colmar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Colmar is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Near it, in 833 CE, the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> deserted to his rebellious sons, an episode known as the &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-of-lies">Field of Lies</a>&quot;. The humiliation of the emperor illustrated the internal conflicts that divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colmar.jpg" alt="Colmar" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sinava-- from Berlin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_%C3%89glise_Saint-Martin_(43833049001).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
